{
  "case_id": "2006-06-116",
  "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is properly before this Court, which should reverse under the plain language and purpose of the Organic Act of Guam. As to jurisdiction, at the time Congress amended the Organic Act to replace the certiorari jurisdiction of the Ninth Circuit with direct review in this Court, the Ninth Circuit had already granted the writ of certiorari that had been timely filed and the case had been briefed, argued and submitted. The amendment said nothing about its application to pending appeals, and someone had to decide whether and how it applied to this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice SCALIA: Mr. Waxman, I thought the Ninth Circuit did decide that question in another case that was pending, Santos."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But if we accept that in the opinion, what was the phrase you used, colorable jurisdiction, or -- it's something I made up, I suppose -- is there some concept that we can refer to or some phrase that works to -- in order to incorporate your test that you seem to be suggesting?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "issues an order withdrawing and deferring a ruling in this case pending the decision in Santos."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question is the following. In Puerto Rico and in the Philippines after 1916, and in Alaska, were there any instances in which they issued bonds that exceeded the 10 percent of the assessed value as opposed to the aggregate market value?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman (petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the plainest meaning is the meaning, we respectfully submit, the most natural meaning of \"tax valuation\" is the valuation that is used by Guam for the calculation of tax."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Beth S. Brinkmann (respondent)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case should be dismissed for want of jurisdiction because the certiorari petition filed in this Court to review the judgment of the Guam Supreme Court was untimely. If the Court were nonetheless to reach the merits of the opinion of the case, the opinion of the Guam Supreme Court interpreting section 11 of the Organic Act should be affirmed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What if, what if you have an ambiguous statute where it really is not clear whether it applies to pending cases or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BRINKMANN: No, Your Honor. That would include the tax-exempt property. That would be a much larger number."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Because?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BRINKMANN: Because that property in Guam is still securing this debt to a certain degree. It is property that must be valued for tax purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But it doesn't have to be 100 percent. They could change what you call the tax valuation from 100 percent of the fair value to 150 percent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, you say without any responsibility to the voters. I mean, the voters are going to know that if the valuation is changed and the tax rate isn't, their taxes are going up. So I assume the voters are going to be vigilant to what is going on and I assume they have telephones and they'll call their representatives. Why is this -- why do you posit this sort of failure of representative democracy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Miss Brinkmann, just to follow up on Justice Scalia's question, is there any history of the Federal government having to bail out the Guam government for bankruptcy or anything close to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-06-116",
